#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/Writing-An-Async-Node-With-Asyncio-Python.rst:2
msgid "Writing an async node with asyncio (Python)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/Writing-An-Async-Node-With-Asyncio-Python.rst:4
msgid ""
"**Goal:** Create and run a service and client using ``AsyncNode``, the "
"asyncio-native node API."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/Writing-An-Async-Node-With-Asyncio-Python.rst:6
msgid "**Tutorial level:** Intermediate"
msgstr "**教學等級：** 中級"

#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/Writing-An-Async-Node-With-Asyncio-Python.rst:8
msgid "**Time:** 20 minutes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/Writing-An-Async-Node-With-Asyncio-Python.rst:12
msgid "Contents"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/Writing-An-Async-Node-With-Asyncio-Python.rst:15
msgid "Background"
msgstr "背景"

#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/Writing-An-Async-Node-With-Asyncio-Python.rst:17
msgid ""
"``AsyncNode`` is an asyncio-native alternative to the executor based "
"``Node`` you used in the beginner tutorial. This lets you ``await`` other "
"async operations from inside a ROS 2 callback without blocking the rest of "
"the node."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/Writing-An-Async-Node-With-Asyncio-Python.rst:20
msgid ""
"Beyond services and clients, ``AsyncNode`` supports timers, subscriptions, "
"and publishers as well. Callbacks can be either ``async def`` coroutines or "
"regular ``def`` functions. Keep in mind that a sync callback can't ``await`` "
"anything."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/Writing-An-Async-Node-With-Asyncio-Python.rst:26
msgid "Actions are not yet supported."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/Writing-An-Async-Node-With-Asyncio-Python.rst:30
msgid ""
"Async support already exists in ``Node``: entities accept ``async def`` "
"callbacks, and futures from ``client.call_async()`` can be awaited (see "
"`client_async_callback example <https://github.com/ros2/examples/blob/"
"rolling/rclpy/services/minimal_client/examples_rclpy_minimal_client/"
"client_async_callback.py>`__). Where ``AsyncNode`` differs is in the "
"underlying runtime: callbacks run on the ``asyncio`` event loop rather than "
"rclpy's custom executor, allowing it to natively compose with other "
"libraries within the ``asyncio`` ecosystem."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/Writing-An-Async-Node-With-Asyncio-Python.rst:34
