#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/Writing-An-Async-Node-With-Asyncio-Python.rst:55
msgid "2 Write the service node"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/Writing-An-Async-Node-With-Asyncio-Python.rst:57
msgid ""
"Inside the ``ros2_ws/src/python_async_node/python_async_node`` directory, "
"create a new file called ``async_service.py`` and paste the following code "
"within:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/Writing-An-Async-Node-With-Asyncio-Python.rst:59
msgid ""
"import asyncio\n"
"\n"
"from example_interfaces.srv import Trigger\n"
"import rclpy\n"
"from rclpy.experimental import AsyncNode\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"class TriggerServer(AsyncNode):\n"
"\n"
"    def __init__(self):\n"
"        super().__init__('trigger_server')\n"
"        self._service = self.create_service(\n"
"            Trigger, 'trigger', self._callback\n"
"        )\n"
"\n"
"    async def _callback(self, _request, response):\n"
"        self.get_logger().info('Incoming trigger request')\n"
"        await self.get_clock().sleep(2.0)\n"
"        response.success = True\n"
"        response.message = 'Slept for 2.0s'\n"
"        return response\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"async def _async_main():\n"
"    with rclpy.init():\n"
"        node = TriggerServer()\n"
"        await node.run()\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"def main():\n"
"    asyncio.run(_async_main())\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"if __name__ == '__main__':\n"
"    main()"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/Writing-An-Async-Node-With-Asyncio-Python.rst:98
msgid "2.1 Examine the code"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/Writing-An-Async-Node-With-Asyncio-Python.rst:100
msgid ""
"The first ``import`` statements pull in ``asyncio``, ``rclpy``, the "
"``AsyncNode`` class from ``rclpy.experimental``, and the ``Trigger`` service "
"type."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/Writing-An-Async-Node-With-Asyncio-Python.rst:102
msgid ""
"import asyncio\n"
"\n"
"from example_interfaces.srv import Trigger\n"
"import rclpy\n"
"from rclpy.experimental import AsyncNode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/Writing-An-Async-Node-With-Asyncio-Python.rst:110
msgid ""
"The ``TriggerServer`` class inherits from ``AsyncNode`` instead of ``Node``. "
"Its constructor initializes the node with the name ``trigger_server`` and "
"creates a service."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/Writing-An-Async-Node-With-Asyncio-Python.rst:113
msgid ""
"class TriggerServer(AsyncNode):\n"
"\n"
"    def __init__(self):\n"
"        super().__init__('trigger_server')\n"
"        self._service = self.create_service(\n"
"            Trigger, 'trigger', self._callback\n"
"        )"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/Writing-An-Async-Node-With-Asyncio-Python.rst:123
msgid ""
"The service callback is a coroutine. Inside it you can ``await`` any async "
"operation — here the node calls ``self.get_clock().sleep(2.0)``, similar to "
"``asyncio.sleep`` but with ROS sim time support. While this coroutine is "
"suspended, the node remains responsive to other callbacks."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/Writing-An-Async-Node-With-Asyncio-Python.rst:127
msgid ""
"async def _callback(self, _request, response):\n"
"    self.get_logger().info('Incoming trigger request')\n"
"    await self.get_clock().sleep(2.0)\n"
"    response.success = True\n"
"    response.message = 'Slept for 2.0s'\n"
"    return response"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/Writing-An-Async-Node-With-Asyncio-Python.rst:136
msgid ""
"The bottom of the file defines an ``async`` helper that initializes "
"``rclpy``, constructs the node, and runs it:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/Writing-An-Async-Node-With-Asyncio-Python.rst:138
msgid ""
"async def _async_main():\n"
"    with rclpy.init():\n"
"        node = TriggerServer()\n"
"        await node.run()"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/Writing-An-Async-Node-With-Asyncio-Python.rst:145
msgid ""
"To run an ``AsyncNode``, you need to ``await node.run()`` — the equivalent "
"of ``rclpy.spin(node)``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/Writing-An-Async-Node-With-Asyncio-Python.rst:147
msgid ""
"Finally, ``main`` itself is a regular sync function so that ``ros2 run`` can "
"use it as an entry point — ``ros2 run`` invokes the entry point as a regular "
"function, so it cannot be ``async def``. It just calls ``asyncio.run`` to "
"execute the ``_async_main`` coroutine:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/Writing-An-Async-Node-With-Asyncio-Python.rst:150
msgid ""
"def main():\n"
"    asyncio.run(_async_main())"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/Writing-An-Async-Node-With-Asyncio-Python.rst:156
msgid "3 Write the client node"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/Writing-An-Async-Node-With-Asyncio-Python.rst:158
msgid ""
"Inside the ``ros2_ws/src/python_async_node/python_async_node`` directory, "
"create a new file called ``async_client.py`` and paste the following code "
"within:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/Writing-An-Async-Node-With-Asyncio-Python.rst:160
msgid ""
"import asyncio\n"
"\n"
"from example_interfaces.srv import Trigger\n"
"import rclpy\n"
"from rclpy.experimental import AsyncNode\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"async def _async_main():\n"
"    with rclpy.init():\n"
"        async with AsyncNode('trigger_client') as node:\n"
"            client = node.create_client(Trigger, 'trigger')\n"
"\n"
"            node.get_logger().info('Waiting for trigger service...')\n"
"            await client.wait_for_service()\n"
"            node.get_logger().info('Service is available, sending request')\n"
"\n"
"            request = Trigger.Request()\n"
"            response = await client.call(request)\n"
"\n"
"            node.get_logger().info(\n"
"                f'Service responded: success={response.success}, '\n"
"                f'message=\"{response.message}\"'\n"
"            )\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"def main():\n"
"    asyncio.run(_async_main())\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"if __name__ == '__main__':\n"
"    main()"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/Writing-An-Async-Node-With-Asyncio-Python.rst:195
msgid "3.1 Examine the code"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/Writing-An-Async-Node-With-Asyncio-Python.rst:197
msgid ""
"As with the service code, the imports pull in ``asyncio``, ``rclpy``, "
"``AsyncNode``, and the ``Trigger`` type."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/Writing-An-Async-Node-With-Asyncio-Python.rst:199
msgid ""
"The client uses the second ``AsyncNode`` entry point: ``async with "
"AsyncNode(...) as node:``. Entering the ``async with`` block is what "
"actually runs the node — analogous to ``await node.run()`` on the server "
"side. At that point any subscriptions, services, and timers that were "
"already created on the node start dispatching callbacks. The node keeps "
"running for the duration of the block, and when the block exits "
"``destroy_node()`` is called automatically and all entities are torn down. "
"This is the right choice for short programs like a one shot client."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/Writing-An-Async-Node-With-Asyncio-Python.rst:205
msgid ""
"async with AsyncNode('trigger_client') as node:\n"
"    client = node.create_client(Trigger, 'trigger')"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/Writing-An-Async-Node-With-Asyncio-Python.rst:210
msgid ""
"Before sending the request, ``await client.wait_for_service()`` suspends the "
"coroutine until a matching service is discovered (or returns immediately if "
"one is already up) — without blocking the event loop, so other callbacks on "
"the node continue to run. This avoids the \"client started before the "
"server\" failure mode where a request would otherwise be sent into the void."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/Writing-An-Async-Node-With-Asyncio-Python.rst:213
msgid ""
"node.get_logger().info('Waiting for trigger service...')\n"
"await client.wait_for_service()\n"
"node.get_logger().info('Service is available, sending request')"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/Writing-An-Async-Node-With-Asyncio-Python.rst:219
msgid "The actual service call is one line:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/Writing-An-Async-Node-With-Asyncio-Python.rst:221
msgid ""
"request = Trigger.Request()\n"
"response = await client.call(request)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/Writing-An-Async-Node-With-Asyncio-Python.rst:226
msgid ""
"With ``AsyncNode`` the response is awaited directly — there is no "
"``Future``, and the node continues to process other work while the call is "
"in flight."
msgstr ""

