#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/Writing-An-Async-Node-With-Asyncio-Python.rst:406
msgid ""
"Replace the body of ``async_service.py`` so that the ``Trigger`` callback "
"delegates to ``demo_nodes_py``'s ``add_two_ints`` service:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/Writing-An-Async-Node-With-Asyncio-Python.rst:408
msgid ""
"import asyncio\n"
"\n"
"from example_interfaces.srv import AddTwoInts, Trigger\n"
"import rclpy\n"
"from rclpy.experimental import AsyncNode\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"class TriggerServer(AsyncNode):\n"
"\n"
"    def __init__(self):\n"
"        super().__init__('trigger_server')\n"
"        self._client = self.create_client(AddTwoInts, 'add_two_ints')\n"
"        self._service = self.create_service(\n"
"            Trigger, 'trigger', self._callback\n"
"        )\n"
"\n"
"    async def _callback(self, _request, response):\n"
"        self.get_logger().info('Waiting for add_two_ints service...')\n"
"        await self._client.wait_for_service()\n"
"\n"
"        self.get_logger().info('Calling add_two_ints with a=2, b=2')\n"
"        nested_request = AddTwoInts.Request(a=2, b=2)\n"
"        nested_response = await self._client.call(nested_request)\n"
"\n"
"        response.success = True\n"
"        response.message = f'2+2={nested_response.sum}'\n"
"        return response\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"async def _async_main():\n"
"    with rclpy.init():\n"
"        node = TriggerServer()\n"
"        await node.run()\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"def main():\n"
"    asyncio.run(_async_main())\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"if __name__ == '__main__':\n"
"    main()"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/Writing-An-Async-Node-With-Asyncio-Python.rst:452
msgid ""
"The client is created in ``__init__`` and used inside the callback. Because "
"the call is awaited, the coroutine doesn't block the node — other callbacks "
"continue to make progress while it waits for ``add_two_ints`` to respond."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/Writing-An-Async-Node-With-Asyncio-Python.rst:457
msgid ""
"The standard ``Node`` utilizes :doc:`callback groups <../../How-To-Guides/"
"Using-callback-groups>` to manage callback execution. Any attempt to perform "
"a service call from within a callback with the default "
"``MutuallyExclusiveCallbackGroup`` would result in deadlocking the node. "
"With ``AsyncNode``, all callbacks run cooperatively on the ``asyncio`` event "
"loop, so ``await client.call(request)`` works from any callback without "
"additional configuration."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/Writing-An-Async-Node-With-Asyncio-Python.rst:461
msgid "Run the underlying ``add_two_ints`` server in one terminal:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/Writing-An-Async-Node-With-Asyncio-Python.rst:463
msgid "$ ros2 run demo_nodes_py add_two_ints_server"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/Writing-An-Async-Node-With-Asyncio-Python.rst:467
msgid "Restart your service and run the client as before:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/Writing-An-Async-Node-With-Asyncio-Python.rst:473
msgid ""
"$ ros2 run python_async_node client\n"
"[INFO] [trigger_client]: Service responded: success=True, message=\"2+2=4\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/Writing-An-Async-Node-With-Asyncio-Python.rst:479
msgid "Handling requests concurrently"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/Writing-An-Async-Node-With-Asyncio-Python.rst:481
msgid ""
"By default, async services process one request at a time — if a callback is "
"still running when a new request arrives, the new one waits."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/Writing-An-Async-Node-With-Asyncio-Python.rst:483
msgid ""
"Passing ``concurrent=True`` dispatches each incoming request on its own "
"task, enabling multiple callbacks to run in parallel:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/Writing-An-Async-Node-With-Asyncio-Python.rst:485
msgid ""
"self._service = self.create_service(\n"
"    Trigger, 'trigger', self._callback, concurrent=True\n"
")"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/Writing-An-Async-Node-With-Asyncio-Python.rst:491
msgid ""
"With concurrent dispatch, three clients arriving at the same time each get "
"their response after roughly two seconds rather than queueing up. The same "
"flag is available on ``create_subscription``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/Writing-An-Async-Node-With-Asyncio-Python.rst:495
msgid "Summary"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/Writing-An-Async-Node-With-Asyncio-Python.rst:497
msgid ""
"You wrote an async service and client using ``AsyncNode``, with ``async "
"def`` callbacks that can ``await`` long running operations. Because "
"``AsyncNode`` runs on ``asyncio``, your node can directly use the rest of "
"the Python async ecosystem — web frameworks, messaging clients, database "
"drivers, and more."
msgstr ""
